From bd726d63962b2fc4bbc3f202c0c4c916eb6dcaff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:36:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harbor_agent): pi adapter, the standalone release
 uploaded into the sandbox

PiNemoGym (custom_agents/pi_nemo_gym.py) runs the pi coding agent
(github.com/earendil-works/pi, v1.5.2) inside the task sandbox against the
Gym model server, like OpenCodeNemoGym:

- install: the release archive (Bun-compiled binary, no Node) is uploaded
  from pi_archive_dir, sha256-checked on the node and in the sandbox; only
  the binary, package.json and README.md are unpacked to /opt/pi-nemo-gym.
- run: one recorded command (installed_compat) that writes models.json,
  settings.json and the turn-budget extension into /logs/agent/pi-agent and
  runs `pi --print --mode json` with stdin from /dev/null; events go to
  agent/pi.txt, the session to agent/pi/sessions.
- capture: compaction, auto-retry, cache warming, HTTP timeouts, extensions,
  MCP, skills, prompt templates and project .pi/ files are off; provider
  compat keeps the request to model/messages/tools/stream/max_tokens (no
  store, reasoning_effort, developer role, session headers, cache key).
- max_turns: an extension that blocks the tool calls of the last allowed
  turn with terminate, so pi stops without another model call.
- no ATIF trajectory (the model server's capture holds the rollout).

failure_classes.pi_end_flags reads agent/pi.txt with the rules of
opencode_end_flags (shared as _context_end_flags; OpenCode's messages are
unchanged); app.py uses it when the trial has pi.txt and no flags file.
deep_merge, verified_archive and the pipefail/kill constants move to
installed_compat (OpenCode imports them from there). README: pi in
"Agents inside the sandbox" and "Failure classes".

Checked against the pi v1.5.2 source (commit b4afdddf); not yet run
against a real pi binary or model.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
