+**pi** ([github.com/earendil-works/pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi), `PiNemoGym`): the standalone release
+(a Bun-compiled binary, no Node) is uploaded from `pi_archive_dir` into each sandbox and only the binary and its
+`package.json` are unpacked (the image needs `tar`). The run writes pi's `models.json` (one OpenAI-compatible
+provider at `api_base`), `settings.json` and the optional turn-budget extension into `/logs/agent/pi-agent` and
+runs `pi --print --mode json` with the tools `read`, `bash`, `edit`, `write`; the events go to `agent/pi.txt`, the
+session to `agent/pi/sessions`. For capture the adapter turns off compaction (summary calls, compact-and-retry),
+pi's auto-retry (it re-sends a prompt and drops the failed attempt), cache warming, the HTTP timeouts,
+extensions, MCP, skills, prompt templates and project-local `.pi/` files, and keeps the request to `model`,
+`messages`, `tools`, `stream`, `stream_options` and `max_tokens` (provider `compat`; pi would otherwise send
+`store`, `reasoning_effort` and the system prompt as role `developer` to an unknown endpoint). pi sends no
+sampling parameters: use `sampling_overrides` as for OpenCode. `max_turns` becomes an extension that blocks the
+tool calls of the last allowed turn, so pi stops without one more model call. In `--mode json` pi exits 0 also
+when its last call failed; the failure classes read `agent/pi.txt` instead.
+
+```yaml
+harbor_agent_name: null
+harbor_agent_import_path: "responses_api_agents.harbor_agent.custom_agents.pi_nemo_gym:PiNemoGym"
+harbor_model_base_url: http://127.0.0.1:8000        # the tunnel's sandbox end
+harbor_agent_kwargs:
+  version: 1.5.2
+  pi_archive_dir: /path/to/pi                       # <dir>/<version>/pi-linux-x64.tar.gz
+  pi_timeout_sec: 1740                              # below harbor_agent_max_timeout, so the verifier still runs
+  max_turns: 100
+  model_info:
+    max_input_tokens: ${policy.max_total_sequence_length}
+    max_output_tokens: ${policy.generation.max_new_tokens}
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `version` | `1.5.2` | pi release. Settings, flags and the extension API were checked against this release; another one needs `pi_sha256` and a re-check. |
+| `pi_archive_dir` | required | Directory with `<version>/<asset>`. The archive's sha256 is checked once per process, and again in the sandbox if `sha256sum` is there. |
+| `pi_asset` | `pi-linux-x64.tar.gz` | Release asset (glibc x86_64, built for `bun-linux-x64-baseline`: no AVX2 needed). |
+| `pi_sha256` | built in for 1.5.2 | sha256 of the archive. |
+| `pi_timeout_sec` | none | pi is ended with exit 124 after this, so its log and exit status are recorded before Harbor's agent timeout. |
+| `pi_workdir` | none | Absolute path pi runs in (created if missing); unset = the image's working directory. |
+| `pi_settings` | `{}` | Deep-merged last into pi's `settings.json`; `null` deletes a key. |
+| `max_turns` | none | Model calls per episode. |
+| `model_info` | `{}` | `max_input_tokens` / `max_output_tokens`: pi's `contextWindow` / `maxTokens`, and the context limit for failure classes. |
+
